{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns","id":1019731,"title":"Armor versus special attacks that aren't guns...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T05:54:00-08:00","id":1019731,"title":"Armor versus special attacks that aren't guns...","content":"Say my Mage who is using his fate Arcana Armor (3 fate+5 defense) fights a Vampire in bat swarm form (which when he attacks ignores defense) attacks my Mage. Do I have any armor. The fact my Armor applies to firearms implies its special... do I get to apply my 3 at least or nothing? Storyteller call?<br /> <br /> Say I have the same armor up and someone shoots me I DO apply my whole armor right, not just the 3... correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T06:11:26-08:00","id":1019735,"title":"","content":"Against the vampire you'd have 3 armor and no Defense. Against a gun you would have Defense 5 and an armor rating of 3, Defense and armor aren't the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:02:48-08:00","id":1019776,"title":"","content":"Assuming 2E rules Defense and Armor are not the same as said before. Generally speaking defense discribes the ability of a character to move out of harms way, while armor is some protective element that absorbs damage, when you are already hit. Even though the attainment is called &quot;Fate Armor&quot; it doesn't actually give any armor, but additional defense. Defense can normally not be applied against firearm attacks, since a normal human is to slow to react to bullets. There are some execptions which give the ability to use defense against fire arms, like most Werewolfforms, which have quicker instincts and reflexes or some of the armor attainments, because: magic.<br /> An attack which explicitely does not apply defense, won't apply the additional defense from the attainment either. I guess you just can't move out of the way if you are completely sourrunded by bats. If you on the other hand have any armor, a kevlar vest e.g., that would apply, since the bats cannot gnaw through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T08:16:53-08:00","id":1019781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019735#post1019735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against the vampire you'd have 3 armor and no Defense. Against a gun you would have Defense 5 and an armor rating of 3, Defense and armor aren't the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apparently I wasn't clear the Fate Mage Armor attainment... which provide your arcanum rating as a bonus to defense... was what I was writing about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","user":"yrtalien","date":". 12-20-2016, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:27:48-08:00","id":1019816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>yrtalien</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019781#post1019781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently I wasn't clear the Fate Mage Armor attainment... which provide your arcanum rating as a bonus to defense... was what I was writing about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fate Armor gives you +[Fate] to your Defense and allows you to use your Defense against Firearms. The Swarm Form Merit allows a vampire to make a Strength + Brawl attack that ignores the target's Defense. No, Fate Armor does not allow you to retain your Defense against attacks made by swarms, because they are not Firearms attacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T09:34:29-08:00","id":1019819,"title":"","content":"Which makes sense if you consider that the various Mage Armors were designed to not have one be the only one worth having. Dealing with the swarm would probably be better served by Life or Death.<br /> <br /> Although, Mind Armor is possibly quite ridiculous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:16:10-08:00","id":1019965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019816#post1019816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate Armor gives you +[Fate] to your Defense and allows you to use your Defense against Firearms. The Swarm Form Merit allows a vampire to make a Strength + Brawl attack that ignores the target's Defense. No, Fate Armor does not allow you to retain your Defense against attacks made by swarms, because they are not Firearms attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'm going to have to disagree with this interpretation and say that even though it specifies Firearm attacks, this is one of those situations where the rules weren't written with the abilities of other supernaturals in mind when the wording was decided on.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would recommend looking at how it logically works and deciding based on that whether it would apply or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T14:40:58-08:00","id":1019981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019965#post1019965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think I'm going to have to disagree with this interpretation and say that even though it specifies Firearm attacks, this is one of those situations where the rules weren't written with the abilities of other supernaturals in mind when the wording was decided on.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would recommend looking at how it logically works and deciding based on that whether it would apply or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Fate Armor adds to your Defense and let's you apply Defense against Firearms because it makes attacks coincidentally miss you. Swarm Form ignores the target's defense because they're so surrounded by small, hostle animals there is nowhere they can move that isn't occupied by more small, hostile animals. Therefore, Fate Armor shouldn't allow you to apply your Defense against it because no matter how lucky you are you're still surrounded by small, hostile animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T15:27:58-08:00","id":1020006,"title":"","content":"In a way, being surrounded by a swarm is closer to a grapple situation than a gun situation. Especially when most swarms that start biting you tend to actually be climbing on you and your clothes, rather than just nipping at your heels. <br /> <br /> Should Fate let you add Defense against grapples? I'm personally against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:22:52-08:00","id":1020199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019981#post1019981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure. Fate Armor adds to your Defense and let's you apply Defense against Firearms because it makes attacks coincidentally miss you. Swarm Form ignores the target's defense because they're so surrounded by small, hostle animals there is nowhere they can move that isn't occupied by more small, hostile animals. Therefore, Fate Armor shouldn't allow you to apply your Defense against it because no matter how lucky you are you're still surrounded by small, hostile animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but something like Mind shield also wouldn't work against it, because it too is a Defense boost that that particular power would ignore, even though logically, you're still dealing with a bunch of thinking creatures with which should still be forced to hesitate and made reluctant to attack, as per the reasoning of the ability. Hell, it would work against the Space shield, even though it specifically works by bending space and forcing attacks to miss through that.<br /> <br /> Again, the wording of abilities weren't written with other splats in mind, so how various powers interact should probably be taken with a grain of salt. Personally, I'd just Clash it to make it simple. That or let it get rid of the normal defense but have the magical aspect still apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:26:36-08:00","id":1020201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020006#post1020006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a way, being surrounded by a swarm is closer to a grapple situation than a gun situation. Especially when most swarms that start biting you tend to actually be climbing on you and your clothes, rather than just nipping at your heels.<br /> <br /> Should Fate let you add Defense against grapples? I'm personally against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I'd liken it more to being surrounded by a bunch of guys all trying to dog pile and grapple you at once. Would Fate magic let you add your defense in that situation? I'd say yes myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:47:29-08:00","id":1020202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020201#post1020201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'd liken it more to being surrounded by a bunch of guys all trying to dog pile and grapple you at once. Would Fate magic let you add your defense in that situation? I'd say yes myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ummm... I'm having an headache how a guy can accidently and coincidentally dodge attacks, even in that situation you just described. Help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:50:48-08:00","id":1020203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020199#post1020199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, the wording of abilities weren't written with other splats in mind</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire's application of the Swarm Form Merit to combat works by rolling the attack and distributing successes amongst characters within the area. The effect is similar to how Beast doesn't have the generic mechanics for swarms but provides similar rules for the Infestation Atavism. Neither implies that their rules serve as particularly special types of swarm that merit discounting the narrative role of a swarm of animals.<br /> <br /> Mage specifically addresses &quot;some characters turn into swarms of animals&quot; in the section on the Life Arcanum and suggests modeling the dangers of a swarm as an Extreme Environment (presumably 4, given the company the effect is keeping) against viable targets.<br /> <br /> If you can't dodge a sandstorm, you can't dodge being covered in bees. That's what Armor and Shielding spells are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T23:59:21-08:00","id":1020205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020201#post1020201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'd liken it more to being surrounded by a bunch of guys all trying to dog pile and grapple you at once. Would Fate magic let you add your defense in that situation? I'd say yes myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Each attack reduces your Defense by 1 for the rest of the turn. Eventually, if enough guys attack you, you won't have any Defense left, even with Fate armor. Swarm Form simply abstracts all of those attacks into one single roll and says you don't get Defense against it, on account of the roll represent a whole bunch of attacks, each making the next harder to avoid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T03:50:19-08:00","id":1020259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020201#post1020201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I'd liken it more to being surrounded by a bunch of guys all trying to dog pile and grapple you at once.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not trying. They've already succeeded. That's kind of the whole point of the analogy - you are already grappled, and people in a grapple can't use Defense to avoid damage from the grappler using a Damage maneuver. I was mainly pointing out that there are melee situations where Defense just doesn't apply. Just because you can dodge bullets doesn't mean you can dodge a flood. <br /> <br /> Hells, its even questionable if Fate Armor will still work if someone uses maneuvers like Cheap Shot on a Fate-mage, if you're Blinded, or if the mage in question sacrifices Defense through an All Out Attack. Strictly by the rules, it does not. Mage armors work against surprise attacks. That is a specific line called out as an exception. Fate, Time, Mind and Space specifically call out that that they apply against Firearm attacks, while Life does not. Exceptions to normal Defense rules are called out. Even if you want to argue that Cheat Shot should be considered an exception, since its not plausable to list every merit that may deny Defense or that it relies on a kind of surprise attack (a feint), you can't argue the same for combat Tilts or sacrificing Defense. Those are as much a part of the general rules as Surprise attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T09:15:30-08:00","id":1020431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020202#post1020202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ummm... I'm having an headache how a guy can accidently and coincidentally dodge attacks, even in that situation you just described. Help?</div> </div> </div> </div>By magically twisting Fate to cause them to get in each others way, slip up, and any other manner of coincidental method of missing. Pretty basic stuff actually. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020203#post1020203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what Armor and Shielding spells are for.</div> </div> </div> </div>After thinking it over after getting some sleep, I agree with this. This is, probably, what additional shielding spells are for. Specifically something to either repel swarms or make it so that Defense doesn't lower by any means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:20:31-08:00","id":1020473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020431#post1020431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, probably, what additional shielding spells are for. Specifically something to either repel swarms or make it so that Defense doesn't lower by any means.</div> </div> </div> </div> Satchel compared a Swarm Form to a sandstorm. Can you use Defense against a sandstorm while in the middle of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:27:56-08:00","id":1020476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020473#post1020473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Satchel compared a Swarm Form to a sandstorm. Can you use Defense against a sandstorm while in the middle of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>With shielding magic? I don't see why not. It's what they're for.<br /> <br /> Edit: Thinking about it, that's probably more Perfecting magic rather than Shielding, though shielding can be used to no sell it for less effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:38:30-08:00","id":1020486,"title":"","content":"How and why can you apply Defense (ie dodging and weaving out of the way of something) against a sandstorm? Narratively, it makes absolutely no sense. Sure, a mage can create a ward where sand can't pass, can harden skin or create a force field, can use magic to speed zirself out of the way of the storm. But, that's not what we're talking about. We're talking about using Defense. So, in narrative terms, how does Defense work against something that is literally all around you? Duck out of the way of some sand, and you hit more sand by the same movement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T10:55:30-08:00","id":1020495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020486#post1020486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How and why can you apply Defense (ie dodging and weaving out of the way of something) against a sandstorm? Narratively, it makes absolutely no sense. Sure, a mage can create a ward where sand can't pass, can harden skin or create a force field, can use magic to speed zirself out of the way of the storm. But, that's not what we're talking about. We're talking about using Defense. So, in narrative terms, how does Defense work against something that is literally all around you? Duck out of the way of some sand, and you hit more sand by the same movement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally? It wouldn't, because tilts don't 'attack'. Though as you've mentioned, you can use magic to limit it's effect. So if you really wanted to 'dodge', you could force it into clustered patterns that could be avoided. Though like I said, it'd be easier to no sell it completely rather than making it able to be dodged, though it is still something you could do.<br /> <br /> Though the more relevant issue here is that a swarm isn't an environmental tilt. Even in swarm form they still have to attack and can still miss. Environmental tilts don't ignore your defense or reduce it in any way. In fact, the tilt doesn't attack at all, and defense is only relevant against attacks. Since swarms do, they can have defense applied to them with the right spell in effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:14:46-08:00","id":1020510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020495#post1020495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though the more relevant issue here is that a swarm isn't an environmental tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said nothing about Tilts and what I did say anything about applies a global penalty to everyone inside along with damage over time.<br /> <br /> Mage's presented mechanics for swarms don't have them engaging in combat attacks; that a power in Vampire uses the mechanics of full characters to represent the use of &quot;turn into a swarm of rats/bats/bugs/etc&quot; as an offensive measure doesn't override the fact that Defense is not applicable against area-wide effects or other sources of damage with no reasonable means of escape.<br /> <br /> Again, you want <i>Armor</i> for that. This is an Attainment we're talking about \u2014 effects that don't simply modify your spellcasting should be relatively subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:20:19-08:00","id":1020515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020510#post1020510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said nothing about Tilts and what I did say anything about applies a global penalty to everyone inside along with damage over time.<br /> <br /> Mage's presented mechanics for swarms don't have them engaging in combat attacks; that a power in Vampire uses the mechanics of full characters to represent the use of &quot;turn into a swarm of rats/bats/bugs/etc&quot; as an offensive measure doesn't override the fact that Defense is not applicable against area-wide effects or other sources of damage with no reasonable means of escape.<br /> <br /> Again, you want <i>Armor</i> for that. This is an Attainment we're talking about \u2014 effects that don't simply modify your spellcasting should be relatively subtle.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't say it was a tilt, and I never said you did. I was talking about MCNs sandstorm analogy, which would be represented by an environmental tilt.<br /> <br /> I haven't been specifically talking about just the Attainment since your last point. I agreed that that alone wouldn't cut it, and that it would take additional spellwork to let it apply. I'm talking about how with that additional spellwork it would allow it to work just fine, though even then I admit it would be easier to no sell the method of attack completely rather than simply allow you to apply Defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:38:45-08:00","id":1020521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020495#post1020495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a swarm isn't an environmental tilt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it can be. There's a Swarm Tilt in Demon on page 179. Mage says on Page 151 that Swarms can't make conventional attacks but might count as Extreme Environments. Unfortunately, the Swarm rules are just not very standardized in 2e. We have at least three different sources on them, all of which function similarly but with slight differences. That said, all of them are capable of damaging creatures within them in a way that ignores Defense, and 2 of the 3 versions deal damage without making actual attack rolls at all. It would be pretty weird if Fate Armor allowed you to use your Defense against a Swarm of bees when it's a transformed Gangrel, but not when it's a transformed Thyrsus, or when it's actual bees that have either been coaxed into attacking by a Demon's Exploit, or simply pissed off because you fucked with their hive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T11:50:02-08:00","id":1020528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020521#post1020521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually it can be. There's a Swarm Tilt in Demon on page 179. Mage says on Page 151 that Swarms can't make conventional attacks but might count as Extreme Environments. Unfortunately, the Swarm rules are just not very standardized in 2e. We have at least three different sources on them, all of which function similarly but with slight differences. That said, all of them are capable of damaging creatures within them in a way that ignores Defense, and 2 of the 3 versions deal damage without making actual attack rolls at all. It would be pretty weird if Fate Armor allowed you to use your Defense against a Swarm of bees when it's a transformed Gangrel, but not when it's a transformed Thyrsus, or when it's actual bees that have either been coaxed into attacking by a Demon's Exploit, or simply pissed off because you fucked with their hive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then it can be, but in this case it isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:21:19-08:00","id":1020552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020528#post1020528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then it can be, but in this case it isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're the one who said,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1019965#post1019965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would recommend looking at how it logically works and deciding based on that whether it would apply or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>If two out of three versions of the swarm mechanics don't even make actual attacks, and the third says it denies the opponent their defense, it's not very logical if you can use Mage Armor to apply Defense against swarms when they're really vampires but not against any other kind of swarm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-21-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T12:50:18-08:00","id":1020573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020552#post1020552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one who said,<br /> <br /> <br /> If two out of three versions of the swarm mechanics don't even make actual attacks, and the third says it denies the opponent their defense, it's not very logical if you can use Mage Armor to apply Defense against swarms when they're really vampires but not against any other kind of swarm.</div> </div> </div> </div>An argument with which I conceded.<br /> <br /> And for the last time, I specifically said that no, the Mage Armor Attainment alone <i>wouldn't</i> cut it. It would take at least one additional spell, probably one designed specifically to allow Defense to be applied to things at times it normally wouldn't, for it to be applicable. And just because it works a particular way with one power doesn't mean it works the same way for all similar (though markedly different) powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T13:29:30-08:00","id":1020603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020573#post1020573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An argument with which I conceded.<br /> <br /> And for the last time, I specifically said that no, the Mage Armor Attainment alone <i>wouldn't</i> cut it. It would take at least one additional spell, probably one designed specifically to allow Defense to be applied to things at times it normally wouldn't, for it to be applicable. And <b>just because it works a particular way with one power doesn't mean it works the same way for all similar (though markedly different) powers.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to have to disagree in this case on the bolded part. Just because it's a vampire's Swarm Form Merit and not a Mage's Shapechanging or an actual swarm of bees shouldn't mean one swarm of animals shouldn't function the same way as another swarm of the same animals. Again, though, that's more a problem of Swarm rules not being standardized than anything, which is why I just stick to the Swarm Tilt for anything involving swarms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:02:16-08:00","id":1020631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020603#post1020603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to have to disagree in this case on the bolded part. Just because it's a vampire's Swarm Form Merit and not a Mage's Shapechanging or an actual swarm of bees shouldn't mean one swarm of animals shouldn't function the same way as another swarm of the same animals. Again, though, that's more a problem of Swarm rules not being standardized than anything, which is why I just stick to the Swarm Tilt for anything involving swarms.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're free to do at your table what you please, but the way that the vampire power works is clearly defined and different from that of Mages, which is different from that of Demons. They might be similar, but they all have their various pros and cons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:10:01-08:00","id":1020640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020631#post1020631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you're free to do at your table what you please, but the way that the vampire power works is clearly defined and different from that of Mages, which is different from that of Demons. They might be similar, but they all have their various pros and cons.</div> </div> </div> </div>But like... Why is a swarm of bats that a vampire turned into different than a swarm of bats that a Mage turned into?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:16:22-08:00","id":1020644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020640#post1020640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But like... Why is a swarm of bats that a vampire turned into different than a swarm of bats that a Mage turned into?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Vampire magic is different than Mage magic? A Vampires affinity for bats is different from a Mages affinity for bats? It's a Mystery? I mean I can throw out possible reasons until I'm blue in the face, but at the end of the day it's just one of those things that they do differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 12-21-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:27:21-08:00","id":1020652,"title":"","content":"Eh. Either way, it's clear you don't get Defense against swarms, in any of the (for some reason) three different sets of rules for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:30:43-08:00","id":1020654,"title":"","content":"At base? No. Which is why I suggested magic to change that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T14:38:01-08:00","id":1020656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020654#post1020654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At base? No. Which is why I suggested magic to change that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What magic do you suggest?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T15:14:24-08:00","id":1020670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020656#post1020656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What magic do you suggest?</div> </div> </div> </div>A spell that let's you apply your defense to things you normally couldn't, or that makes it so your defense isn't reduced by multiple attacks. Space should be able to do it, Forces should be able to do it, Time, Mind against thinking creatures, etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T17:00:58-08:00","id":1020711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020670#post1020670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A spell that let's you apply your defense to things you normally couldn't, or that makes it so your defense isn't reduced by multiple attacks. Space should be able to do it, Forces should be able to do it, Time, Mind against thinking creatures, etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a Perfecting Life spell that makes you able to perceive and react to every single critter in a swarm. Actually, that sounds like something a Life mage will try at least once. Your examples still sound less like enhancing one's ability to dodge attacks, and more like repelling attacks with a barrier.<br /> <br /> Still, it seems we're agreeing that applying Defense to a swarm is clearly <i>not normal</i>, and would require obviously <i>extraordinary </i>means to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T21:57:43-08:00","id":1020776,"title":"","content":"To me, the storyteller system isn't DnD 3.5. I liked DnD 3.5, I owned many of its books, but it was a system about mechanics. Rules lawyers went to court with each other and DM's sat over events like a reigning Judge. People would pull out examples of X book, page number X, paragraph Y, proves my point, and the other player would point out examples in other books that directly contradicted what the previous book said, leading on to debates of publication dates for what super seeded what. And even there was even appeals court when defeated lawyers, eerr I mean players, would call on other respected DM's to try and overturn there tables DM decision. Argh.<br /> <br /> \u200bWoD isn't like that. Its a general set of rules to help you guys play out a story and encourages you to be logical and use what works on the fly. This ones pretty clear cut. Fate armour lets you dodge bullets, awesome, a swarm isn't a bullet, its a giant mass of biological matter surrounding you, poking, biting, cutting and stinging you form every direction, which is why you don't get a dodge. Fate isn't going to help you there. And it doesn't need to. You have other armor options, use those. That's the point.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut if you don't agree with me, that's fine, if its your game, or your ST agrees with you, then run it how you guys like, thats the beauty of this system, do it however you like. But if your ST is disagreeing with you, sure, explain your case, and then accept his judgement, its not DnD 3.5, lets not go down that path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1510-mysticjackal","name":"MysticJackal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1510_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T01:09:52-08:00","id":1020798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1019731-armor-versus-special-attacks-that-aren-t-guns?p=1020711#post1020711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or a Perfecting Life spell that makes you able to perceive and react to every single critter in a swarm. Actually, that sounds like something a Life mage will try at least once. Your examples still sound less like enhancing one's ability to dodge attacks, and more like repelling attacks with a barrier.<br /> <br /> Still, it seems we're agreeing that applying Defense to a swarm is clearly <i>not normal</i>, and would require obviously <i>extraordinary </i>means to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be fair I never said anything about enhancing your own ability to dodge, just that could magic to let you use it against things you wouldn't normally be able to. And yes, we've technically been in agreement that you couldn't <i>normally </i>apply Defense against swarm form since the start, I was just arguing that Mage Armor should count as extraordinary enough to suffice in this situation. After hearing various arguments, I conceded that it wasn't, not on its own anyways (I conceded that point like 10 posts ago actually). It would take additional applications of magic to make it work.<br /> <br /> Though yes, as far as I can tell, everyone is currently in general agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}